## 5. Freshness Classes

### [CXC-FRESH-CLASS] A Named Group That Must ALL Be Current Together

- origin: David, ratifying [D4], verbatim — "or a simple grouping of semantic messages that must all have a specific value within the bounding window defined as a class."
- rule: age is the MAX of the members' ages; the class is UNKNOWN if ANY member is. This is [D4b]'s derived-value rule made a first-class, nameable, YAML-declarable object.
- why-max: a navigation solution is not fresh because its newest input is fresh. It is as old as its OLDEST input, and it is not a solution at all if one input is missing. Taking the max is what stops the freshest member from laundering the staleness of the others.
- it-is-not-a-weaker-fallback: the class was originally deferred on the reading that David offered it as a substitute for per-namespace fields if those proved hard. That reading was too narrow — a per-namespace field cannot express a conjunction ACROSS namespaces at all, so the class is the only form that can state a multi-message contract, and it is where the derived-value rule lives.
- names-the-culprit: the class reports the FIRST unbelievable member's own verdict and can list all of them, because an operator needs to know WHICH sensor died, not merely that the solution is bad.
- empty-is-refused: an empty class would report FRESH forever — a green light wired to nothing. A class naming an unregistered namespace is refused for the same reason: it fails OPEN, reporting FRESH while the namespace nobody registered is the one that died.
- status: implemented
- implementation: python/composeio/freshness.py:FreshnessClass
- verify: python/tests/test_freshness_receiver.py::test_a_freshness_class_is_declarable_in_YAML
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FRESHNESS]

