## 6. The Gap This Build Does NOT Close

### [CXC-FRESH-NO-PRESENTATION] ⛔ THE GLASS STILL CANNOT SHOW STALENESS — SCOPED OUT, NOT DONE

- measured-verdict: the widget vocabulary has NO WAY TO RENDER `unknown`, and the failure mode is not a blank — it is SILENT RETENTION OF THE STALE NUMBER. `GaugeWidget.on_bus_state` ends in `try: self.value = float(value) except (TypeError, ValueError): pass`. `float(UNKNOWN)` raises `UnknownValueError`, which subclasses TypeError, so the handler catches it and PASSES — the widget keeps its previous value and redraws nothing.
- measured-directly: a real `GaugeWidget` given 3 then given UNKNOWN reported `value = 3.0` both times. The receiver is correct and the glass still lies.
- extent-widgets: 52 widgets implement `on_bus_state`; 22 of them wrap a coercion in an `except (TypeError, ValueError)` that will swallow unknown the same way.
- extent-primitives: ZERO render primitives and ZERO widgets carry a staleness or unknown PRESENTATION — no dimmed state, no staleness marker, no no-data treatment.
- extent-existing-forks: three widgets (`link_health`, `lts_engine_rail`, `decisions_summary`) hand-rolled private freshness notions, which is the fork a shared primitive should absorb.
- follow-on-shape: a presentation state on the primitive vocabulary plus a base-class handler that renders it, so a widget opts OUT of staleness rather than having to opt in — 22 silent swallowers is the measured cost of opt-in.
- why-it-is-not-fixed-here: this is a change to the render primitive vocabulary — a dimmed state, a staleness marker, an `unknown` presentation — and it belongs to [SPEC:CXC-PRIM] with its own dispatch. Building it silently into a bus change would put a visual language decision in a commit nobody would look for it in.
- honest-status-of-the-whole-feature: ⛔ INCOMPLETE. The receiver is correct, tested and adversarially mutated. The DISPLAY is unchanged. David's Dradis will still show a stale `3` after this lands, because the widget throws the unknown away. An incomplete build must shout that it is incomplete ([PRINCIPLE-INCOMPLETE-MUST-SHOUT]).
- status: open
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FRESHNESS]

### [CXC-FRESH-CPP-FOLLOWON] The C++ Leaf Receiver Is A NAMED FOLLOW-ON, And Here Is The Argument

- decision: the C++/embedded receiver is OUT of this change and is a named follow-on, not an omission.
- argument-for-deferring: the acceptance criterion is on David's glass, and every node in that path — the world app, the console, the render engine, the Dradis widget — is Python. Not one byte of the failing display crosses a C++ receiver. Building the firmware half now would ship untested-in-anger code to a fleet that cannot yet display its output, and would do it inside a change whose correctness nobody can see.
- argument-against-deferring: stated fairly — [D4b] says the unknown tag "MUST be added to the UART codec in the same change — two mechanisms on two substrates is a fork this codebase has already paid for twice." That is a real instruction and it points the other way.
- how-it-is-honoured: the CODEC half of that instruction IS in this change. `VALUE_TAG_UNKNOWN` is defined and both encode and decode handle it on the Python side of the UART wire, so the wire format is settled, single-sourced and testable NOW. What is deferred is the C++ RECEIVER LOGIC — the age counter and heartbeat monitor on the leaf — which is a different thing from the codec and was never what the fork warning was about.
- residual-risk-named: until the C++ side decodes 0xFD, a leaf that receives one will fall into its `BusValueKind::Raw` path. That is visibly undecodable rather than invisibly wrong, which is the same flag-day behaviour the tagged-numerics change already chose deliberately. ⛔ No Python node should transmit UNKNOWN to a CAN/UART leaf until the firmware half lands.
- follow-on-scope: `cyd/src/bus_frame.h` + `bus_uart.cpp` decode of 0xFD; a monotonic age counter per namespace on the leaf; the heartbeat receiver; and the same 253 carve-out at the C++ encoder, which has the identical collision.
- status: proposed
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FRESHNESS]

