## 7. What The Spec Prose Got Wrong

### [CXC-FRESH-SPEC01-CORRECTION] `spec/01` Described The Receiver As LIVE, Which Is Why It Was Believed Built

- defect: `spec/01-composeio-bus-protocol.smd` sections 2.5, 5.2 and 9.2 describe heartbeat cadence and heartbeat-timeout-driven degraded mode as working behaviour, carrying NO not-implemented banner — while seven-plus other places in the same document do carry one. The reader's inference was therefore correct and the document was wrong.
- consequence: this is precisely why David believed the freshness receiver had been built. The false claim was not incidental to the defect; it was the mechanism by which the defect stayed unfixed.
- rule-this-establishes: a spec section describing unbuilt behaviour must be banner-marked, and a document that banners SOME of its unbuilt sections makes every unbannered section a positive claim of implementation.
- migration-boundary: `spec/01` is corrected but NOT migrated, held by the ruling that migration CONFERS AUTHORITY — migrating a stale spec does not carry the staleness forward, it LAUNDERS it. This node is the LTS-tier statement of the corrected behaviour; the `.smd` carries a pointer here rather than a re-description.
- status: implemented
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FRESHNESS]

